difference between scheduling optimization and ESO:

"Point-to-point predictive routing... if your region has the required map coverage level"
How it works:

Legacy Engine: Frequently relied on straight-line ("as the crow flies") aerial distance multiplied by an average speed, or
generic street-level routing without dynamic conditions.

ESO Engine: Uses Point-to-Point Predictive Routing. It maps the actual turn-by-turn road network and integrates historical, 
time-of-day traffic patterns (e.g., driving 10 miles at 8:30 AM takes 35 minutes, but the same route at 1:00 PM takes 15 minutes).
     

